  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the summer, nitrogen dioxide and methane react with chlorine monoxide and chlorine atoms which results in a shrinkage of chlorine and hence prevents ozone layer depletion.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi><mover><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mo>&#8729;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>ClO</mi><munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>During winter, special types of clouds are formed over the Antarctic region. These clouds provide the surface for the hydrolysis of chlorine nitrate to form hypochlorous&nbsp;acid.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClONO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HOCl</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ClONO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>HOCl</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p>"
